welcomed राम and कृष्ण and fulfilled their desire by restoring सान्दिपानि's son; presented पृठु with a rod of justice. Punished नृग to be a lizard for having given a cow of a ब्रह्मण as a gift to another, and as the owner refused to accept the apologies and compensation offered by नृग;
3: Ib. X. ४५. ४२-6; IV. १५. १५; III. ३०. २३; X. ६४. १६-24.
